WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:01.794
- Night owls like myself, we're just

00:00:01.794 --> 00:00:05.240
full of vodka and like
nachos or something.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.194
(upbeat string music)
(wolf howling)

00:00:12.025 --> 00:00:15.222
- I usually go to bed maybe
around one every night.

00:00:15.222 --> 00:00:16.958
- Between like 12 and two.

00:00:16.958 --> 00:00:19.223
- Anywhere between 12 and 3am.

00:00:19.223 --> 00:00:21.379
- I wake up for work as
late as I possibly can

00:00:21.379 --> 00:00:24.072
to still get there on
time and in one piece.

00:00:24.072 --> 00:00:25.803
- I hit snooze five or six times

00:00:25.803 --> 00:00:27.150
before getting up in the morning.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.426
- I desperately want
to be a morning person.

00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:31.376
- I love the idea of people getting up,

00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:34.395
like walking their dogs,
and like being healthy,

00:00:34.395 --> 00:00:36.890
and eating granola and yogurt.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.874
- I could be a much more productive person

00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:41.686
if I utilized those morning hours.

00:00:41.686 --> 00:00:43.682
- I'm about to wake up early as (bleep),

00:00:43.682 --> 00:00:45.447
and I'm really excited but nervous

00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:46.840
that I won't be able to do it.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:51.579
(upbeat music)

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:53.017
- [Voiceover] Hey, Kelsey.

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:54.178
- Hey, what's up?

00:00:55.736 --> 00:00:58.195
- I do. I get up around 3:30 every day.

00:00:59.277 --> 00:01:00.983
- I power lift and I prefer to train

00:01:00.983 --> 00:01:02.893
in the morning as opposed to the evening.

00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:05.906
Honestly, it's a better, like
more healthy way of living.

00:01:05.906 --> 00:01:07.729
I have more time in the day.

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:09.029
I can get more stuff done.

00:01:09.029 --> 00:01:10.887
I'm not as rushed, and honestly

00:01:10.887 --> 00:01:12.361
our ancestors lived that way.

00:01:12.361 --> 00:01:14.509
They woke up with the sun
and went to bed with the sun,

00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:17.295
so for me, it's the more
natural way of living.

00:01:19.187 --> 00:01:22.340
- Yeah, I would love to help
some night owls wake up early.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:24.058
Rule number one is--

00:01:24.058 --> 00:01:24.968
- No!

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.195
- Oh!
(laughs)

00:01:26.195 --> 00:01:28.136
- Monday through Friday, you need

00:01:28.136 --> 00:01:30.365
to be up by 5am.

00:01:30.365 --> 00:01:32.176
Saturday and Sunday, I would prefer

00:01:32.176 --> 00:01:33.848
if you were up by eight o'clock.

00:01:33.848 --> 00:01:36.077
Rule number two, with your extra time

00:01:36.077 --> 00:01:37.377
in the morning, do something that you

00:01:37.377 --> 00:01:38.724
love to do, that you don't normally

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:39.648
have time to do.

00:01:39.648 --> 00:01:40.893
- Like walking my dog.

00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:42.613
- Cook a serious breakfast maybe.

00:01:42.613 --> 00:01:44.716
Number three is, this is Sunday night

00:01:44.716 --> 00:01:46.063
through Thursday night, you need

00:01:46.063 --> 00:01:48.338
to be in bed between nine and 11.

00:01:48.338 --> 00:01:51.915
Friday and Saturday night, 10pm to 1am,

00:01:51.915 --> 00:01:53.666
because I know people like to go out.

00:01:53.666 --> 00:01:54.688
- I'm gonna have no life!

00:01:54.688 --> 00:01:56.129
Nothing gets started until ten.

00:01:56.129 --> 00:01:58.555
- Ok. Let's get into it!

00:01:58.555 --> 00:01:59.902
- Let's do it, guys!

00:01:59.902 --> 00:02:01.016
- I think you guys can do it.

00:02:01.016 --> 00:02:02.117
I think you'll surprise yourself

00:02:02.117 --> 00:02:03.378
in another two weeks.

00:02:03.378 --> 00:02:05.323
- Let's go! Whoo!
- Whoo!

00:02:05.323 --> 00:02:08.354
- I'm going to bed way
later than I wanted to,

00:02:08.354 --> 00:02:11.233
but the night just kind
of got away from me.

00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:13.415
- My goal is to wake up tomorrow

00:02:13.415 --> 00:02:15.120
and work out before work.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.409
I'm optimistic. I'm excited.

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:20.103
I hope that I can do this.

00:02:20.103 --> 00:02:22.285
- I failed my first night.

00:02:22.285 --> 00:02:24.083
Today we'll do better though.

00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.408
I'm like a mess in the morning, holy shit!

00:02:26.408 --> 00:02:28.601
- Actually I don't feel that tired.

00:02:28.601 --> 00:02:31.387
Upon a very short conversation
with my boyfriend,

00:02:31.387 --> 00:02:33.895
I realized I'm in a
really bad mood! (laughs)

00:02:33.895 --> 00:02:37.935
I am just incapable of communicating

00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:40.025
properly with other humans.

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:42.845
- I had time for a little
bit of stretching and yoga,

00:02:42.845 --> 00:02:45.969
and I'm also gonna have
time to do my hair.

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:49.638
(car alarm blaring)

00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:51.867
- It's 10am on a Saturday.

00:02:51.867 --> 00:02:53.446
Much too early for me,

00:02:53.446 --> 00:02:54.978
so we headed to Starbucks

00:02:54.978 --> 00:02:56.592
for some much-needed caffeine

00:02:56.592 --> 00:02:59.297
and I'm so cranky about it!

00:02:59.297 --> 00:03:02.956
- So, I'm at work. Sleepy as fuck.

00:03:02.956 --> 00:03:05.056
Basically, I've been
failing, as of lately.

00:03:05.056 --> 00:03:06.436
Well, no.

00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:08.585
The weekend I woke up really early.

00:03:08.585 --> 00:03:10.164
- So, we're supposed to get up super early

00:03:10.164 --> 00:03:13.043
for our breakfast tomorrow,
but I'm exhausted.

00:03:13.043 --> 00:03:14.356
We'll see how it goes.

00:03:14.356 --> 00:03:15.347
I mean, I have to do it.

00:03:15.347 --> 00:03:16.632
It will be the worst thing ever

00:03:16.632 --> 00:03:17.690
if I somehow don't make it.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:21.124
- I am absolutely miserable.

00:03:21.655 --> 00:03:23.122
- You're such a drama queen.

00:03:23.122 --> 00:03:24.404
- No one is up this early!

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.203
- Look, there are plenty of people out.

00:03:26.203 --> 00:03:27.936
- There are four people here.

00:03:27.936 --> 00:03:31.980
- I'm actually doing chores
before the sun's out!

00:03:32.301 --> 00:03:33.765
What!

00:03:33.765 --> 00:03:35.366
- I just realized that the new episode

00:03:35.366 --> 00:03:37.502
of Scream Queens is on Hulu,

00:03:37.502 --> 00:03:39.313
so I'm actually gonna try to catch

00:03:39.313 --> 00:03:42.053
a little bit of it, pour
myself a tiny glass of wine,

00:03:42.053 --> 00:03:45.350
even though the rules say I shouldn't.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.844
I wanted to be just like
my friends on Instagram,

00:03:47.844 --> 00:03:50.412
and I failed miserably.

00:03:50.412 --> 00:03:51.991
- I have been getting up earlier,

00:03:51.991 --> 00:03:53.570
so in the mornings I'm more relaxed.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.090
It's a better start to the day,

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:56.728
and I just feel like I'm in a better mood.

00:03:56.728 --> 00:03:58.214
- The first week I definitely noticed

00:03:58.214 --> 00:04:00.232
that my body would be up, but my brain

00:04:00.232 --> 00:04:02.997
wouldn't be up with me at the same time.

00:04:02.997 --> 00:04:05.319
Waking up and doing something physical

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:07.362
and centering, like
yoga, definitely helped

00:04:07.362 --> 00:04:10.613
me get both of my halves
started with the day.

00:04:10.613 --> 00:04:13.167
- I enjoy my night life so much,

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.243
and the fact that conversations

00:04:15.243 --> 00:04:18.229
would just be getting good at like 11

00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:19.901
and I was already late to bed

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.155
was kind of a weird thing.

00:04:21.155 --> 00:04:22.501
- I definitely think
that people who consider

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:25.475
themselves night owls should
try waking up earlier.

00:04:25.475 --> 00:04:27.935
Maybe even just by like an hour or so.

00:04:27.935 --> 00:04:31.278
It feels really good to not
be rushed in the morning.

00:04:31.278 --> 00:04:34.423
- I'd really like to make
this like a legit life change.

00:04:34.423 --> 00:04:37.501
Where I actually become
a real morning person.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:39.684
- Ugh. Goodbye night life.

00:04:39.684 --> 00:04:41.402
It's been nice knowing you.

00:04:41.402 --> 00:04:42.470
I'm gonna start hanging out

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.844
with morning moms now.

00:04:45.303 --> 00:04:49.129
(upbeat music)

